    "cage": {
      "word": "CAGE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A box or inclosure, wholly or partly of openwork, in wood or metal, used for confining birds or other animals. In his cage, like parrot fine and gay. Cowper.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A place of confinement for malefactors Shak. Stone walls do not a prison make, Nor iron bars a cage. Lovelace.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Carp.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "An outer framework of timber, inclosing something within it; as the cage of a staircase. Gwilt.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mach.) (a) A skeleton frame to limit the motion of a loose piece, as a ball valve. (b) A wirework strainer, used in connection with pumps and pipes.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The box, bucket, or inclosed platform of a lift or elevator; a cagelike structure moving in a shaft.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Mining)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The drum on which the rope is wound in a hoisting whim.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Baseball)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The catcher's wire mask.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To confine in, or as in, a cage; to shut up or confine. \"Caged and starved to death.\" Cowper.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
